<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><br><br>GD77 does not require a DFU driver becuase in DFU mode the radio mimics being  "Human Interface device" and Windows has a built in driver for this.<br><br>Does your GD77 already have OpenGD77 installed, or does it currently have the official firmware installed ?<br>I ask becuase there are bugs in the GD77 DFU which can prevent the radio being updated, which are caused by bugs in the official firmware</div></blockquote>the firmware installed is 20231231193513 in the gd-77's that i am trying to upgrade.</div></blockquote>OK.<br><br>If the same cable works on a UV380, it should be OK on the GD77<br><br>Look in the windows device manager, and open the HID branch and count the number of devices, then plug in the GD77 when its in DFU mode and then recount and there should be one more device.<br><br>If not then Windows is not seeing the radio</div></blockquote>Under the HID branch I have 4 usb input devices, and when i set the radio in firmware upload mode i get a 5th one.  Windows beeps when connected.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2530">W8LDO</a> — Sat Sep 28, 2024 1:47 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
